WEBVTT

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:11.333
<i>Fluttering and dancing in the sky</i>

00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:17.708
<i>Let our love reach you...</i>

00:00:17.708 --> 00:00:18.458
<i>LOVE,</i>

00:00:18.458 --> 00:00:19.542
<i>LOVE,</i>

00:00:19.542 --> 00:00:20.958
<i>LOVE...</i>

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.000
<i>ohhhh... SAY!</i>

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.417
<i>This heart</i>

00:00:26.417 --> 00:00:28.708
<i>Try and move it</i>

00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:31.833
<i>Look, how should I show you?</i>

00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:33.000
<i>Then together with us</i>

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.375
<i>Let's dance! Take my hand</i>

00:00:34.375 --> 00:00:35.833
<i>hey yeah yeah!</i>

00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:37.333
<i>Leave it to me</i>

00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:40.250
<i>to escort you! ALL RIGHT!</i>

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.958
<i>As if worrying, the passing rain</i>

00:00:42.958 --> 00:00:46.417
<i>caressed my cheek gently,</i>
<i>so as not to be noticed.</i>

00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:50.375
<i>Jumping over faster than a shooting star</i>

00:00:50.375 --> 00:00:53.833
<i>Reach out your hand!</i>

00:00:53.833 --> 00:00:54.750
<i>let's get LOVE!</i>

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:56.375
<i>Shout to the moon! (shout!)</i>

00:00:56.375 --> 00:00:58.000
<i>Let your shout ring out! (shout!)</i>

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.167
<i>What's up, what's up?</i>

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:00.917
<i>Let me hear your voice</i>

00:01:00.917 --> 00:01:02.458
<i>Undo your hair</i>

00:01:02.458 --> 00:01:05.458
<i>Saying goodbye to yesterday</i>

00:01:05.458 --> 00:01:06.458
<i>when my eyes were closed</i>

00:01:06.458 --> 00:01:09.000
<i>A single petal fluttering lightly</i>

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.875
<i>Spit it out, SHOUT! (shout!)</i>

00:01:10.875 --> 00:01:12.708
<i>Shout out your feelings! (shout!)</i>

00:01:12.708 --> 00:01:13.458
<i>Isn't it fine</i>

00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:15.583
<i>if nothing is for sure?</i>

00:01:15.583 --> 00:01:16.625
<i>wow yeah!</i>

00:01:16.625 --> 00:01:17.125
<i>That's right</i>

00:01:17.125 --> 00:01:18.958
<i>Let's put away the lies</i>

00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:21.667
<i>Let lots of love reach you</i>

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:28.583
<i>Let lots of love reach you</i>

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:47.042
That was a rough outline of the Six Gravity and
Procellarum joint concert, Full Moon Festival.

00:01:47.042 --> 00:01:48.792
Please check it over.

00:01:56.375 --> 00:01:59.292
Hajime, Shun, do you have anything to add?

00:01:59.292 --> 00:02:06.583
My policy is to show Procella and Gravi
at their best and most perfect on any stage.

00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:08.750
That's good to hear.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.917
What about you, Hajime?

00:02:10.917 --> 00:02:12.042
Hajime?

00:02:12.042 --> 00:02:14.833
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:16.667
I think it's very good.

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:22.000
I think what the fans imagine
and desire is taking proper shape.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.375
Is that right?

00:02:23.375 --> 00:02:26.792
Then we'll flesh it out from the outline.

00:02:26.792 --> 00:02:28.917
Thank you, please do.

00:02:33.833 --> 00:02:35.917
Shun, you're going straight back
to the dorms, right?

00:02:35.917 --> 00:02:36.833
What about you, Hajime?

00:02:36.833 --> 00:02:39.042
If you have to go to a job, I can drop you off.

00:02:39.042 --> 00:02:42.917
This is all Hajime has today, too,
so the dorms is fine.

00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:43.958
Okay.

00:02:43.958 --> 00:02:46.917
Dai, Kanade, can I have a moment?

00:02:46.917 --> 00:02:48.250
What is it, Shun?

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:53.083
About this... Can I take it home
for now, just in case?

00:02:53.083 --> 00:02:57.458
I want to ask the others their opinion
about the set list and everything else.

00:02:57.458 --> 00:03:00.000
Black King, what do you think?

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.042
I also ask to do the same.

00:03:05.042 --> 00:03:09.167
Please allow me to discuss the set list
and the rest with the others.

00:03:12.208 --> 00:03:14.708
Oh, it's finally here!

00:03:14.708 --> 00:03:15.875
Welcome home.

00:03:15.875 --> 00:03:18.000
Oh, it's Haru's essence!

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.750
What? There are two of Haru's essence?!

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.833
You two really like that schtick, huh?

00:03:23.833 --> 00:03:26.208
What's with those glasses?

00:03:26.208 --> 00:03:28.958
Oh, did you get a new pair for the concert?

00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:32.542
No, I sent them out to be repaired
and just got them back.

00:03:32.542 --> 00:03:37.125
They were broken by a giant rabbit at the
cottage we went to over the summer, remember?

00:03:38.875 --> 00:03:41.875
Then, what about the glasses
you're wearing right now?

00:03:41.875 --> 00:03:44.000
They're my spare glasses.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.583
You've been wearing them since then?

00:03:45.583 --> 00:03:48.583
I used them when we had the blackout
on the island, too, remember?

00:03:48.583 --> 00:03:50.333
Yeah, now that you mention it....

00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:54.167
I mean, they're the same, right?
The same glasses.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.708
They fit differently.

00:03:58.417 --> 00:04:01.667
Hmm, is that the pickiness of a glasses maniac?

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:03.583
We're home.

00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:05.458
Welcome back!

00:04:05.458 --> 00:04:08.042
Thanks. I'm calling a meeting.

00:04:14.458 --> 00:04:18.000
Well, I guess I understand
what you two are saying.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.875
The good part is that it's like us.

00:04:20.875 --> 00:04:23.375
What about the bad part?

00:04:23.375 --> 00:04:25.750
It's a little too much like us.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:28.000
There's nothing objectionable about it, right?

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.167
It feels unoriginal.

00:04:30.167 --> 00:04:33.500
It's important to follow the theory, though.

00:04:34.583 --> 00:04:38.500
It does feel like it's doing
what it's supposed to.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.500
But something's missing...

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:48.167
The Full Moon Festival is an
important turning point for us.

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:53.167
But more than that, I think it's
also a dream performance

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:56.542
that the fans who have supported us
all this time have been waiting for.

00:04:56.542 --> 00:04:59.292
I don't want to compromise an inch.

00:04:59.292 --> 00:05:00.833
I don't think we should.

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:02.792
That's why...

00:05:02.792 --> 00:05:04.833
I want you to lend me your strength.

00:05:08.375 --> 00:05:09.958
Hajime...

00:05:09.958 --> 00:05:13.000
I can't believe you're relying on us!

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.875
It might be the first time!

00:05:16.708 --> 00:05:19.167
Looks like fun, doesn't it?

00:05:19.167 --> 00:05:20.208
Yeah.

00:05:20.208 --> 00:05:22.917
Getting even more serious than usual, huh?

00:05:22.917 --> 00:05:25.458
Of course I'm planning on giving it my all.

00:05:25.458 --> 00:05:28.250
Because this is <i>our </i>concert.

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:35.542
Yeah, I don't want to regret not
doing everything I should have.

00:05:35.542 --> 00:05:36.625
Kai...

00:05:36.625 --> 00:05:39.833
What's this? It sounds like
there's a deeper meaning to that.

00:05:39.833 --> 00:05:42.750
I know! What about this?

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:47.875
Let's make limited edition Tsukiusa bunnies
like you did for the Animate store event

00:05:47.875 --> 00:05:51.417
and shoot them out of bazookas and into
the audience at the end of the concert!

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:55.125
It'd be nice to have a variety segment
with lots of fun jokes, huh?

00:05:55.125 --> 00:05:58.250
Oh, like Kai Fuduki's Spear-Fishing Dojo?

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:00.500
What's a spear-fishing dojo?

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:03.208
Like a soba-making dojo?

00:06:03.208 --> 00:06:06.833
Yeah, yeah! You're good
at spear fishing, right, Kai?

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:09.458
No, wait, it's not like I'm good at it or anything.

00:06:09.458 --> 00:06:11.917
It was just necessary at the time.

00:06:11.917 --> 00:06:16.542
And what about having everyone do
an improvised song when they're introduced?

00:06:16.542 --> 00:06:17.542
Improvised song?

00:06:17.542 --> 00:06:20.000
I can't do anything like that.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.292
That's a good idea!

00:06:21.292 --> 00:06:25.833
In the show I was just in,
Super Dimension Robot: Ultimate Black Wing,

00:06:25.833 --> 00:06:29.167
each robot had its own theme song.

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:32.250
Their names were in the lyrics.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:33.583
Isn't that awesome?

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:38.792
Oh, so we'd put our names in the lyrics?

00:06:38.792 --> 00:06:41.958
Yeah! Like, since my name means "love,"

00:06:41.958 --> 00:06:45.875
it'd be: "Love, love, love!
Love, love, love you!"

00:06:45.875 --> 00:06:46.833
or something.

00:06:46.833 --> 00:06:48.250
Wow...

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:50.833
Putting "love, love you" aside,

00:06:50.833 --> 00:06:53.875
since the twelve of us have a
chance to be on stage together,

00:06:53.875 --> 00:06:58.792
wouldn't it be nice to have something special
that we can only do with all of us?

00:06:58.792 --> 00:07:02.417
Something we can only do with all of us?

00:07:02.417 --> 00:07:05.083
Something we can do because
all twelve of us are together...

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:11.167
You look like you've already got
something in mind, huh, Hajime?

00:07:11.167 --> 00:07:12.833
Huh? Really?

00:07:12.833 --> 00:07:15.875
Did you think of something, Hajime?

00:07:16.458 --> 00:07:18.083
"Proposal '12-Person Song'"

00:07:18.083 --> 00:07:18.875
"Proposal '12-Person Song'"
Huh?

00:07:18.875 --> 00:07:20.958
"Proposal '12-Person Song'"
A song the twelve of you will sing together?

00:07:20.958 --> 00:07:26.792
Yes, we were hoping to perform a new song
with Gravi and Procella together.

00:07:26.792 --> 00:07:28.333
Isn't it wonderful?

00:07:28.333 --> 00:07:32.500
It's a special present we can only give
with all twelve of us together.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:35.250
It is, but it's so sudden.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:38.250
"Set List"

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.958
I understand how you feel.

00:07:41.958 --> 00:07:44.958
I think it's a very compelling idea.

00:07:47.083 --> 00:07:51.917
There's still time to prepare the dance
and staging for the new song.

00:07:51.917 --> 00:07:53.083
But...

00:07:53.083 --> 00:07:56.542
The problem is whether a song
can be written in time...

00:07:56.542 --> 00:07:58.458
Yeah...

00:07:58.458 --> 00:08:05.958
I'm sure you both know that the president of
Tsukino Talent Production, Mikoto Tsukino,

00:08:05.958 --> 00:08:08.500
writes all the Gravi and
Procella group songs himself.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:11.875
However, the president has been
especially busy recently.

00:08:11.875 --> 00:08:15.167
It's hard to imagine that he
would have time to do that.

00:08:15.167 --> 00:08:18.833
We will pass this proposal on to the president,

00:08:18.833 --> 00:08:22.375
but it's hard to say whether or not
he'll have time to look at it...

00:08:23.375 --> 00:08:24.708
I understand.

00:08:24.708 --> 00:08:27.208
Sorry to concern you.

00:08:27.208 --> 00:08:30.750
Can I ask for one more thing?

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.125
Hajime?

00:08:32.125 --> 00:08:38.875
Please ask the concert staff to leave
a space for the new song in the set list.

00:08:40.167 --> 00:08:41.708
Hey, but--

00:08:41.708 --> 00:08:43.750
Dai, Kanade.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:47.458
It appears our king is resolved to do this.

00:08:47.458 --> 00:08:49.583
And so am I.

00:08:49.583 --> 00:08:53.792
I plan to go along with his
fervent desire to take action this time.

00:08:53.792 --> 00:08:54.750
Huh?

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:57.042
Wh-What are you planning?

00:08:57.042 --> 00:09:01.458
We will speak with the president
directly and get his consent.

00:09:01.458 --> 00:09:05.292
We will prepare a new song
by any means necessary.

00:09:56.583 --> 00:09:57.333
"I'm heading to the reception desk"
"Sorry"

00:09:57.333 --> 00:09:58.583
"Thanks"
"No good today, either"

00:09:58.833 --> 00:10:00.875
Aw, no luck, huh?

00:10:00.875 --> 00:10:02.417
Is that from Haru?

00:10:02.417 --> 00:10:03.958
What did he say?

00:10:03.958 --> 00:10:05.750
"I couldn't see him today, either.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:09.083
And actually, it looks like the
president isn't even in Tokyo."

00:10:09.083 --> 00:10:10.208
What?

00:10:10.208 --> 00:10:11.417
I'm home!

00:10:12.167 --> 00:10:13.250
I'm home!

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.583
Excuse me.

00:10:14.583 --> 00:10:15.833
Hello!

00:10:15.833 --> 00:10:19.375
Huh? What? It's so gloomy!

00:10:19.375 --> 00:10:21.208
Hey, You.

00:10:21.208 --> 00:10:22.625
What's the matter?

00:10:22.625 --> 00:10:25.792
Couldn't get a hold of
the president today, either?

00:10:25.792 --> 00:10:28.167
You got it, Aoi.

00:10:28.167 --> 00:10:34.583
It looks like he's gone to an event called the
Asian Talent Production Friendship Music Festa.

00:10:34.583 --> 00:10:39.750
Hajime and Haru just sent a message saying
they didn't know when he would be back.

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:43.750
I can see why everyone's gloomy.

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:48.083
We're running out of time
to have a new song written.

00:10:48.083 --> 00:10:53.292
We had them include the new song
at the end of the set list for now,

00:10:53.292 --> 00:10:56.458
but it's cutting it pretty close if we think
about the time needed to prepare for it.

00:10:58.333 --> 00:11:01.375
Huh? I got a message from Mattsun.

00:11:01.375 --> 00:11:02.667
From Mattsun?

00:11:02.667 --> 00:11:03.958
Who's that?

00:11:03.958 --> 00:11:06.167
Yoru and my friend from home.

00:11:06.167 --> 00:11:09.208
Didn't he say he was on vacation somewhere?

00:11:09.208 --> 00:11:11.083
Yeah. Let's see...

00:11:11.083 --> 00:11:14.708
"Yay. I saw someone amazing
at the airport earlier.

00:11:14.708 --> 00:11:17.000
He said he's going back to Tokyo now. Yay"...

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:17.542
"Attachment"
He said he's going back to Tokyo now. Yay"...

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:21.417
Huh?!

00:11:21.417 --> 00:11:24.083
T-The president?!

00:11:24.083 --> 00:11:25.500
What?!

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:27.667
Is it okay for something like that to happen?

00:11:27.667 --> 00:11:31.667
Why does your friend know
who the president is?

00:11:31.667 --> 00:11:35.375
Oh, yeah! I showed him a picture of
the agency's New Year's party before!

00:11:35.375 --> 00:11:38.750
I can't believe he remembered what
the president looked like just from that.

00:11:38.750 --> 00:11:41.708
It's no good. Mattsun's not picking up.

00:11:41.708 --> 00:11:43.875
Maybe he's already on the plane.

00:11:43.875 --> 00:11:48.083
What should we do?
This is our chance to catch the president!

00:11:48.083 --> 00:11:51.542
We have no choice but to go to the airport.

00:11:51.542 --> 00:11:53.000
Shun!

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:56.458
Didn't you say you were
sleeping all day today?

00:11:57.833 --> 00:12:01.333
It looked like things were
getting fun out here.

00:12:01.333 --> 00:12:04.333
I hurried back from my dreams.

00:12:04.333 --> 00:12:06.250
Oh, I see...

00:12:08.167 --> 00:12:11.667
Now, you have the proposal, right?

00:12:11.667 --> 00:12:16.375
We'll catch the president of Tsukino
Talent Production, Mikoto Tsukino,

00:12:16.375 --> 00:12:19.333
no matter what it takes.

00:12:19.333 --> 00:12:21.958
--Yeah!
--Y-Yeah!

00:12:30.625 --> 00:12:32.583
Yes, hello?

00:12:32.583 --> 00:12:34.083
What?

00:12:34.083 --> 00:12:35.208
What's wrong?

00:12:35.208 --> 00:12:38.208
He said everyone's heading
to the airport right now.

00:12:38.208 --> 00:12:39.458
Airport?

00:12:39.458 --> 00:12:43.542
To wait for the president
to come out to catch him.

00:13:08.583 --> 00:13:10.042
Oh dear.

00:13:10.042 --> 00:13:11.292
Shun?

00:13:11.292 --> 00:13:13.292
You can never escape, huh, Shun?

00:13:13.292 --> 00:13:16.708
You're stuck again?

00:13:16.708 --> 00:13:18.042
We don't have time to wait.

00:13:18.042 --> 00:13:19.542
Let's go!

00:13:19.542 --> 00:13:20.708
What?!

00:13:20.708 --> 00:13:23.208
We won't waste the sacrifice of you three!

00:13:23.208 --> 00:13:24.625
Later!

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.208
Excuse me, please hurry!

00:13:29.208 --> 00:13:32.042
This looks like it'll take a while.

00:13:32.042 --> 00:13:36.167
Ikkun, Rui, can I leave this to you?

00:13:36.167 --> 00:13:37.125
Huh?

00:13:37.125 --> 00:13:38.542
What?

00:13:40.583 --> 00:13:41.708
Did you find him?

00:13:41.708 --> 00:13:43.083
No...

00:13:43.083 --> 00:13:45.625
Could we have missed him?

00:13:45.625 --> 00:13:48.417
With this crowd, it's possible.

00:13:48.417 --> 00:13:51.542
Anyway, we'll wait here for now.

00:13:51.542 --> 00:13:52.250
Okay!

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:53.667
Right!

00:13:55.542 --> 00:13:56.667
I don't see him.

00:13:56.667 --> 00:13:57.750
Me neither.

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:00.042
What should we do?

00:14:00.042 --> 00:14:02.792
Uduki and... Satsuki?

00:14:02.792 --> 00:14:04.208
Huh?

00:14:06.958 --> 00:14:08.375
What?

00:14:10.917 --> 00:14:11.833
Hey.

00:14:11.833 --> 00:14:13.333
Mikaduki?!

00:14:13.333 --> 00:14:14.792
Why are you here?

00:14:14.792 --> 00:14:18.042
I just got back from a local performance.

00:14:18.042 --> 00:14:20.167
What about you guys? What are you doing?

00:14:20.167 --> 00:14:23.167
Have you seen our agency president?

00:14:23.167 --> 00:14:25.875
I don't know what he looks like.

00:14:25.875 --> 00:14:27.292
Right...

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:33.958
Where is the Asian Talent Production
Friendship Music Festa being held, anyway?

00:14:33.958 --> 00:14:37.500
If we know where it departed from,
we can narrow things down a bit.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:40.333
But we couldn't get any hits
even when we looked it up.

00:14:40.333 --> 00:14:42.667
It's an industry event with no general admission...

00:14:42.667 --> 00:14:45.750
Apparently, it's more like a
networking conference.

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:49.917
The Asian Talent Production
Friendship Music Festa?

00:14:49.917 --> 00:14:52.167
Wouldn't that be an international flight?

00:14:52.167 --> 00:14:53.042
What?

00:14:53.042 --> 00:14:55.333
It's being held in Singapore, right?

00:14:55.333 --> 00:14:59.208
There are some musicians from
my agency who are participating, too,

00:14:59.208 --> 00:15:00.667
so I'm sure of it.

00:15:03.208 --> 00:15:04.375
An international flight?

00:15:04.375 --> 00:15:06.458
Yes, he says he's sure of it.

